    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the derived `ownerSegment` field (`<TIER>_<AREA>`) on the owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `ownerSegment` enum property (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`) to the Owner schema, which generates the field on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 Standalone helper (matching the `AgeBand`/`CityRegion` pattern so MapStruct doesn't treat it as a mapping method) that computes the segment:\n   - **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `MembershipLevel.effective(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - **AREA** = `METRO` when the owner's locality (`CustomerCode.locality`) is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL`. Known-region is detected via `CityRegion.timezone(...) != null`, whose table is exactly those three regions.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired `ownerSegment` via an expression mapping.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for Sydney/NSW, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) pass, and the full test suite is **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
